      <title>‘Crocodiles are possible, but hunger is certain’: Malawi’s foragers forced into infested waters</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/nov/16/malawi-hunger-food-foraging-nyika-shire-river-crocodiles</link>
      <description>Once ‘famine food’, empty granaries have forced people along the Shire River to harvest water-lily roots in waters full of the reptiles The mid-morning heat in Malawi’s lower Shire River basin is already suffocating, but Beatrice Maseko cannot afford to look away from the water’s edge. Coated in grey, foul-smelling mud up to her thighs, the 34-year-old mother of four plunges both arms deep into the heavy sediment of a sprawling marsh. Her fingers feel blindly through the silt for the rough…</description>
