      <title>Warming UK seas could ‘fundamentally reshape marine ecosystems’ – report</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/05/warming-uk-seas-could-fundamentally-reshape-marine-ecosystems-report</link>
      <description>Four-year study warns destabilised marine food webs could jeopardise food security by 2050 Warming seas around the UK and the wider north-east Atlantic could destabilise marine food webs, weaken ocean health and jeopardise food security by 2050, according to a four-year study. Scientists who projected the impact of climate breakdown on four key groups of marine life crucial to maintaining ocean ecosystems in the region said their results challenged assumptions that in middle latitudes, such as…</description>
